{"step_index":127,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-08-25T18:05:33Z","thinking":"**Testing API Response**\n\nOkay, I'm writing tests for the API. My focus right now is on verifying that movie items correctly return the expected `preview_url` and `media_url` values. I'm updating `tests/test_api.py` to ensure this specific behavior is covered.\n\n\n","tool_calls":[{"name":"write_to_file","args":{"CodeContent":"import os\nimport sys\nfrom pathlib import Path\n\n# Ensure root project directory is on sys.path for test runner imports\nPROJECT_ROOT = Path(__file__).resolve().parent.parent\nif str(PROJECT_ROOT) not in sys.path:\n    sys.path.insert(0, str(PROJECT_ROOT))\n\nimport pytest\nfrom fastapi.testclient import TestClient\nfrom app import app\n\nclient = TestClient(app)\n\n\ndef test_health_endpoint():\n    \"\"\"Tests GET /api/health returns 200 OK and expected serverless metadata.\"\"\"\n    response = client.get(\"/api/health\")\n    assert response.status_code == 200\n    data = response.json()\n    assert data[\"status\"] == \"ok\"\n    assert \"StreamWave\" in data[\"platform\"]\n    assert \"environment\" in data\n    assert \"blob_storage_configured\" in data\n    assert \"timestamp\" in data\n\n\ndef test_get_complete_media_catalogue():\n    \"\"\"Tests GET /api/media returns full catalogue array with movie video previews and music URLs.\"\"\"\n    response = client.get(\"/api/media\")\n    assert response.status_code == 200\n    items = response.json()\n    assert isinstance(items, list)\n    assert len(items) == 8\n    for item in items:\n        assert \"id\" in item\n        assert \"title\" in item\n        assert \"type\" in item\n        assert \"genre\" in item\n        assert \"media_url\" in item\n        if item[\"type\"] == \"movie\":\n            assert item[\"preview_url\"] == \"/media/streamwave-preview.mp4\"\n\n\ndef test_movie_preview_url_field():\n    \"\"\"Tests GET /api/media/1 (Cook Off movie) returns preview_url pointing to /media/streamwave-preview.mp4.\"\"\"\n    response = client.get(\"/api/media/1\")\n    assert response.status_code == 200\n    item = response.json()\n    assert item[\"id\"] == \"1\"\n    assert item[\"type\"] == \"movie\"\n    assert item[\"preview_url\"] == \"/media/streamwave-preview.mp4\"\n\n\ndef test_vercel_blob_url_environment_injection(monkeypatch):\n    \"\"\"Tests that setting STREAMWAVE_BLOB_URL injects Vercel Blob storage URL into music items.\"\"\"\n    test_blob_url = \"https://public.blob.vercel-storage.com/demo-test-123.wav\"\n    monkeypatch.setenv(\"STREAMWAVE_BLOB_URL\", test_blob_url)\n\n    response = client.get(\"/api/media/5\")  # Disappear (music)\n    assert response.status_code == 200\n    item = response.json()\n    assert item[\"media_url\"] == test_blob_url\n\n    health_res = client.get(\"/api/health\")\n    assert health_res.json()[\"blob_storage_configured\"] is True\n\n\ndef test_local_fallback_when_no_blob_env(monkeypatch):\n    \"\"\"Tests clean fallback to /media/demo.wav for music when no Blob environment variable is set.\"\"\"\n    monkeypatch.delenv(\"STREAMWAVE_BLOB_URL\", raising=False)\n    monkeypatch.delenv(\"VERCEL_BLOB_AUDIO_URL\", raising=False)\n\n    response = client.get(\"/api/media/5\")  # Disappear (music)\n    assert response.status_code == 200\n    item = response.json()\n    assert item[\"media_url\"] == \"/media/demo.wav\"\n\n\ndef test_media_search_filter_stream():\n    \"\"\"Tests GET /api/media with query=stream.\"\"\"\n    response = client.get(\"/api/media?query=stream\")\n    assert response.status_code == 200\n    items = response.json()\n    assert len(items) > 0\n    assert any(\"stream\" in item[\"description\"].lower() for item in items)\n\n\ndef test_media_type_filter_music():\n    \"\"\"Tests GET /api/media with type=music.\"\"\"\n    music_res = client.get(\"/api/media?type=music\")\n    assert music_res.status_code == 200\n    music = music_res.json()\n    assert len(music) == 4\n    assert all(item[\"type\"] == \"music\" for item in music)\n\n\ndef test_media_type_filter_movie():\n    \"\"\"Tests GET /api/media with type=movie.\"\"\"\n    movie_res = client.get(\"/api/media?type=movie\")\n    assert movie_res.status_code == 200\n    movies = movie_res.json()\n    assert len(movies) == 4\n    assert all(item[\"type\"] == \"movie\" for item in movies)\n    assert all(item[\"preview_url\"] == \"/media/streamwave-preview.mp4\" for item in movies)\n\n\ndef test_media_genre_filter():\n    \"\"\"Tests GET /api/media with genre filter.\"\"\"\n    response = client.get(\"/api/media?genre=Zimdancehall\")\n    assert response.status_code == 200\n    items = response.json()\n    assert len(items) > 0\n    assert all(item[\"genre\"] == \"Zimdancehall\" for item in items)\n\n\ndef test_get_valid_media_detail_id_1():\n    \"\"\"Tests GET /api/media/1 returns media item detail for ID 1.\"\"\"\n    response = client.get(\"/api/media/1\")\n    assert response.status_code == 200\n    item = response.json()\n    assert item[\"id\"] == \"1\"\n    assert item[\"title\"] == \"Cook Off\"\n    assert item[\"type\"] == \"movie\"\n\n\ndef test_get_unknown_media_detail_404():\n    \"\"\"Tests GET /api/media/{media_id} returns 404 for unknown ID.\"\"\"\n    response = client.get(\"/api/media/unknown-id-9999\")\n    assert response.status_code == 404\n    data = response.json()\n    assert data[\"detail\"] == \"Media item not found\"\n\n\ndef test_valid_play_event_movie():\n    \"\"\"Tests POST /api/play-events with valid movie media ID.\"\"\"\n    payload = {\n        \"media_id\": \"1\",\n        \"session_id\": \"sess-test-123\",\n        \"client_timestamp\": \"2026-08-25T17:25:30Z\",\n    }\n    response = client.post(\"/api/play-events\", json=payload)\n    assert response.status_code == 201\n    data = response.json()\n    assert data[\"status\"] == \"recorded\"\n    assert data[\"event\"][\"media_id\"] == \"1\"\n    assert data[\"event\"][\"media_title\"] == \"Cook Off\"\n    assert \"media_url_used\" in data[\"event\"]\n    assert \"server_timestamp\" in data[\"event\"]\n\n\ndef test_play_event_unknown_media_404():\n    \"\"\"Tests POST /api/play-events returns 404 for non-existent media ID.\"\"\"\n    payload = {\n        \"media_id\": \"nonexistent-media-999\",\n        \"session_id\": \"sess-test-456\",\n    }\n    response = client.post(\"/api/play-events\", json=payload)\n    assert response.status_code == 404\n    data = response.json()\n    assert data[\"detail\"] == \"Media item not found\"\n\n\ndef test_play_event_invalid_body_422():\n    \"\"\"Tests POST /api/play-events returns 422 for missing required fields.\"\"\"\n    payload = {\n        \"session_id\": \"sess-test-789\",\n    }\n    response = client.post(\"/api/play-events\", json=payload)\n    assert response.status_code == 422\n","Description":"Update tests/test_api.py to include movie preview_url verification and movie play event tests","Overwrite":true,"TargetFile":"C:\\Users\\dell\\.gemini\\antigravity\\brain\\228fe0bc-0a77-489e-a1ba-57d617247457\\tests\\test_api.py","toolAction":"Updating tests/test_api.py with movie preview tests","toolSummary":"Updating tests/test_api.py with movie preview tests"}}]}
{"step_index":128,"source":"MODEL","type":"GENERIC","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-08-25T18:05:48Z","content":"Created At: 2026-08-25T20:05:48+02:00\nCompleted At: 2026-08-25T20:05:48+02:00\nCreated file file:///C:/Users/dell/.gemini/antigravity/brain/228fe0bc-0a77-489e-a1ba-57d617247457/tests/test_api.py with requested content.\nIf relevant, proactively run terminal commands to execute this code for the USER. Don't ask for permission."}
{"step_index":129,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-08-25T18:05:48Z","tool_calls":[{"name":"write_to_file","args":{"CodeContent":"# StreamWave Serverless Media Platform\n\nAcademic prototype of a serverless media streaming application built for **StreamWave Entertainment** (a fictional Zimbabwean entertainment company). Constructed with **Python 3.12** and **FastAPI**, engineered specifically for deployment on **Vercel Functions** with **Vercel Blob Storage** and **5-Second MP4 Video Preview** support.\n\n---\n\n## 🚀 Key Features & Architectural Highlights\n\n- **Vercel Serverless Native**: Designed without continuous background processes, SQLite, or runtime filesystem writes to respect Vercel's read-only/ephemeral execution model.\n- **Movie Video Preview**: All movie titles (*Cook Off*, *Neria*, *Gonarezhou*, *Shaina*) present a 5-second StreamWave MP4 video preview (`/media/streamwave-preview.mp4`) in a dedicated modal player upon clicking **\"Watch Preview\"**.\n- **Music Audio Demonstration**: Music items continue utilizing the fixed HTML5 audio player (`/media/demo.wav` or Vercel Blob CDN) upon clicking **\"Play Sample\"**.\n- **Zero Media Proxying**: Media audio and video bytes are fetched directly by the browser from static assets or Vercel Blob CDN. Bytes are never proxied through FastAPI serverless endpoints.\n- **FastAPI & Pydantic Validation**: Strict type annotations, security middleware headers, and Pydantic schema validation for all requests and responses.\n- **Structured Logged Playback Events**: `POST /api/play-events` validates media IDs, attaches UTC server timestamps, and emits structured JSON event logs directly to stdout.\n- **StreamWave Responsive UI**: Dark graphite styling (`#121214`), restrained red accent (`#e50914`), clean rectangular media cards, accessible HTML5 video and audio modal players, and `<dialog>` details modal.\n\n---\n\n## 🎥 Movie Video Preview Configuration\n\n- **Asset Path**: `public/media/streamwave-preview.mp4`\n- **Relative URL**: `/media/streamwave-preview.mp4`\n- **Video Specifications**: HTML5 `<video>` player with `controls`, `playsinline`, `preload=\"metadata\"`, black player background (`#000000`), 16:9 aspect ratio, 960px max width, and Replay button display on `ended`.\n\n---\n\n## ☁️ Vercel Blob Integration & Setup\n\nReference Documentation:\n- [Vercel Blob Overview](https://vercel.com/docs/vercel-blob)\n- [Vercel CLI Blob Documentation](https://vercel.com/docs/cli/blob)\n\n### 1. Creating a Vercel Blob Store\n1. Go to your [Vercel Dashboard](https://vercel.com/dashboard).\n2. Select your project (or create a new Vercel project).\n3. Navigate to **Storage** -> **Create Database** -> **Vercel Blob**.\n4. Select **Public** store type and create the Blob store.\n\n### 2. Uploading Demonstration Assets\nOnly non-copyrighted synthesized audio (`public/media/demo.wav`) and the 5-second StreamWave MP4 video (`public/media/streamwave-preview.mp4`) should be uploaded.\n\n```bash\n# Upload via Vercel CLI\nnpx vercel login\nnpx vercel blob upload public/media/streamwave-preview.mp4\n```\n\n---\n\n## 🔒 Security Guidelines\n\n- **Never Commit Tokens**: `.env`, `.env.local`, and token files are ignored by `.gitignore`.\n- **Public Assets**: Only non-copyrighted academic demonstration audio and video previews are uploaded to public storage.\n- **Fallback Mechanism**: If no Blob URL environment variable is present, `app.py` automatically falls back to local static files.\n\n---\n\n## 📂 Project Structure\n\n```\n.\n├── app.py                      # FastAPI application entry point, asset manager & routing\n├── data/\n│   └── media.json              # Read-only Zimbabwean media catalogue\n├── public/\n│   ├── css/\n│   │   └── styles.css          # Dark graphite responsive CSS design & video modal styling\n│   ├── js/\n│   │   └── app.js              # Vanilla JavaScript frontend logic, video player & API client\n│   ├── media/\n│   │   ├── demo.wav            # Generated demonstration WAV audio asset (fallback)\n│   │   └── streamwave-preview.mp4 # 5-second StreamWave MP4 video preview asset\n│   └── index.html              # StreamWave HTML5 web interface with video modal\n├── scripts/\n│   ├── copy_preview_video.py   # Utility locating and copying streamwave-preview.mp4\n│   ├── generate_demo_audio.py  # Python stdlib script generating synthesized WAV chime\n│   └── upload_to_vercel_blob.py # Script uploading demo assets to Vercel Blob storage\n├── tests/\n│   └── test_api.py             # Pytest automated test suite covering routes & video preview URLs\n├── pyproject.toml              # Python 3.12 environment & tool configurations\n├── requirements.txt            # Pinned dependencies (FastAPI, Uvicorn, Pydantic, Pytest, HTTPX)\n├── .gitignore                  # Source control ignore configuration preventing secret leaks\n└── README.md                   # Technical documentation\n```\n\n---\n\n## 🛠️ Local Execution & Testing\n\n### Run Automated Tests\n```bash\npytest tests/test_api.py -v\n```\n\n### Start Development Server\n```bash\nuvicorn app:app --reload --host 127.0.0.1 --port 8001\n```\n\n- Web UI: [http://127.0.0.1:8001](http://127.0.0.1:8001)\n- OpenAPI Swagger Docs: [http://127.0.0.1:8001/docs](http://127.0.0.1:8001/docs)\n","Description":"Update README.md with 5-second MP4 video preview configuration and architecture details","Overwrite":true,"TargetFile":"C:\\Users\\dell\\.gemini\\antigravity\\brain\\228fe0bc-0a77-489e-a1ba-57d617247457\\README.md","toolAction":"Updating README.md with video preview documentation","toolSummary":"Updating README.md with video preview documentation"}}]}
